===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|hin}}, from {{etyl|he|en}} {{m|he|הִין}}, from {{etyl|egy|en}} {{m|egy|hnw||[[jar]], [[unit]] of [[liquid]] [[volume]]}}: <hiero>h:n-nw-w-W22</hiero>

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical|_|units of measure}} A [[former]] [[Hebrew]] [[unit]] of [[liquid]] [[volume]] ([[about]] 3.8 [[L]]).
#* Bible (NIV), Exodus 30:24:
#*: 500 shekels of cassia — all according to the sanctuary shekel — and a '''hin''' of olive oil.

